From: Robert Teller <robert.j.c.teller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026
Subject: [PATCH] bootstrap.sh: stronger dependency-graph guidance for beads creation

The current bootstrap prompt has a single line about dependencies:

    5. Set dependencies where one bead blocks another:
       bd dep add <later-id> <earlier-id> -t blocks

In practice this produces under-wired graphs. Agents write prose like
"Depends on: Phase 1 epic" in stub descriptions, formalize only the
epic-to-epic chain, and miss within-phase child-to-child links. The
result: `bd ready` returns items whose prose-stated prerequisites are
still open — contradicting the readiness rules in
rules/work-item-templates.md ("Prose dependencies that aren't
formalized are a defect — bd ready will surface the item while its
prerequisites are still open").

This patch closes that gap by adding to the prompt:

  1. Granularity guidance — distinguishes epic-to-epic, child-to-child
     cross-phase, and within-phase child-to-child deps, with concrete
     examples of when each matters.
  2. The "prose-must-match-graph" audit rule that work-item-templates.md
     already requires but the prompt didn't operationalize.
  3. A verification step (`bd ready`, `bd dep tree`, `bd lint`) so
     structural gaps surface before the agent declares done.
  4. Multi-file PRD handling — read sibling docs, surface cross-source
     contradictions as decision-type beads, and block downstream work
     on the decision being resolved.
  5. Decision-type bead callout — calls out that decision/spike beads
     typically BLOCK the items their findings will reshape (the prompt
     previously only mentioned feature/chore/bug).

Tested against the cache-insights project: re-running the bootstrap
prompt with this guidance against the same source documents produces
a fully-wired graph in one pass instead of needing two follow-up
audits to catch (a) the within-phase child-to-child gap on Phase 2
beads 0to.9 / 0to.10, (b) coarse epic-only Phase 3 gating that blocked
unnecessary parallelism, and (c) a missed cross-source contradiction
between DESIGN.prd.md and lessons_learned/cli-vs-direct-api.md that
should have produced a decision bead in the original sweep.

Reference: rules/work-item-templates.md "Readiness Checklist" →
"Dependencies formalized" — the rule the original prompt didn't
operationalize.

---
 scripts/bootstrap.sh | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/scripts/bootstrap.sh
+++ b/scripts/bootstrap.sh
@@ -621,6 +621,13 @@
     PROMPT="$PROMPT DO NOT ask questions that are answered in this document."
     PROMPT="$PROMPT Only ask about information that is genuinely missing from the source."
     PROMPT="$PROMPT"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT If the source document lives in a directory with sibling docs (e.g. research.md,"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT lessons_learned/, lexicon.prd.md), READ THOSE TOO. The named source is often"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT one entry point into a larger spec. When sibling docs DISAGREE with the named"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT source, do not silently pick one — surface the contradiction explicitly and,"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT if beads are enabled, create a decision-type bead to resolve it (see step 5"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT below) and block any downstream work the resolution would reshape."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT"
     if [ "$TIER" = "3-scale" ]; then
         PROMPT="$PROMPT Map source content to Scale templates:"
         PROMPT="$PROMPT - architecture.md → Product Guidance (vision, personas, exclusions), tech stack, system diagram, how to run, technology decisions table"
@@ -656,7 +663,25 @@
     PROMPT="$PROMPT 2. Create an EPIC for each phase: bd create 'Phase 1: <name>' --type epic"
     PROMPT="$PROMPT 3. Create CHILD BEADS under each epic: bd create '<feature title>' --type feature --parent <epic-id>"
     PROMPT="$PROMPT 4. Use the correct type: feature (user-facing), chore (infra/config/tests), bug (defects)."
-    PROMPT="$PROMPT 5. Set dependencies where one bead blocks another: bd dep add <later-id> <earlier-id> -t blocks"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    Use --type decision for items that produce findings (spikes, architectural"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    questions, source-document contradictions) — these typically BLOCK the items"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    their findings will reshape."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT 5. Wire dependencies. Granularity matters more than most agents assume:"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT       bd dep add <later-id> <earlier-id> -t blocks"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    - Epic-to-epic deps gate whole phases (cws-epic blocks 0to-epic blocks rk8-epic)."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT      Necessary but not sufficient — children of the gated epic surface together"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT      when the upstream epic closes, even ones that need a specific sibling."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    - Child-to-child cross-phase deps enable parallel start (a Phase 3 forecast bead"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT      that needs only the cold/warm + warmup outputs from Phase 2 should block on"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT      THOSE specific Phase 2 children, not the whole Phase 2 epic)."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    - Within-phase child-to-child deps are REQUIRED whenever one sibling needs"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT      another's output. Without them, bd ready surfaces both as ready simultaneously."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    Audit rule (from rules/work-item-templates.md Readiness Checklist):"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    Every 'depends on' / 'blocks on' / 'after X' / 'requires X' / 'prerequisite'"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    claim you write in a bead description MUST have a matching bd dep add entry."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    Prose without a graph entry is a defect. After creating beads, grep each"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    description for those words and confirm a formal dep entry exists for each match,"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    OR reword the prose as informational ('works alongside X', not 'depends on X')."
     if [ "$TIER" = "3-scale" ]; then
         PROMPT="$PROMPT 6. For Scale tier, use the STUB TEMPLATE from rules/work-item-templates.md for each bead:"
         PROMPT="$PROMPT    - Summary: one sentence (what + why)"
@@ -671,6 +696,14 @@
         PROMPT="$PROMPT 6. Phase 1 beads are ready to work. Later phases are backlog."
     fi
     PROMPT="$PROMPT"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT 8. VERIFY before declaring done. Do not skip this step:"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    - bd ready              — confirm only truly-startable items are returned."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT                              No bead whose prose says 'depends on X' should appear"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT                              while X is still open."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    - bd dep tree <epic-id> — for each epic, confirm the visual tree matches"
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT                              the prose 'Depends on:' lines in child descriptions."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT    - bd lint               — surfaces structural template gaps."
+    PROMPT="$PROMPT"
     PROMPT="$PROMPT Do NOT create a flat list of unrelated beads. Every bead must belong to an epic."
     if [ "$DRY_RUN" = true ]; then
         PROMPT="$PROMPT Since this is a dry run, LIST the bd commands you would run (do not execute them)."

